package "Infrastructure — dispatch" #F3F4F6 {
  class Dispatcher <<dispatch worker>> {
    - _task : asyncio.Task
    + start()
    + stop()
    + running : bool
    - _claim()
    - _fire(row)
    .. at-LEAST-once, the OPPOSITE of ..
    .. PushSender. Takes a LEASE instead of ..
    .. marking a row done, and every firing ..
    .. function re-reads the world and ..
    .. returns without writing if it has ..
    .. already moved on. Holds no timers in ..
    .. memory: dispatch_tasks.due_at IS the ..
    .. schedule ..
  }
}

